(a) whether Government has taken note of the recent archaeological discovery in Thailand of an ancient gold ring bearing an early Indian inscription, which has renewed interest in the maritime trade and cultural links between ancient Tamilakam and Southeast Asia;
(b) the initiatives introduced by Government to undertake archaeological, epigraphic and maritime research on the historical trade routes connecting the Tamil region with Southeast Asian countries; and
(c) the collaborative projects implemented by Government with foreign museums, universities and archaeological agencies for documentation, conservation and study of artefacts associated with ancient Tamil maritime heritage?

(a) whether Government proposes to expand the role of cooperative institutions in seed production, processing, storage, certification and marketing under the Bharatiya Beej Sahakari Samiti Limited (BBSSL);
(b) the support extended by Government for capacity building of PACS, cooperative societies, seed growers and Farmer Producer Organisations engaged in seed production and distribution;
(c) the details of collaborative activities envisaged with ICAR, State Agricultural Universities and Krishi Vigyan Kendras for field demonstrations, multilocation trials and technology transfer through cooperatives; and
(d) whether any roadmap has been prepared for promoting quality seed exports through the cooperative sector and strengthening value chains?
GK

(a) whether Government proposes to expand the use of indigenous GAGAN-enabled satellite navigation technologies for fixed-wing aircraft and helicopter operations to reduce dependence on conventional ground-based navigation infrastructure;
(b) the initiatives introduced by Government to establish satellite-based instrument approach procedures at airports and heliports, particularly in regions experiencing adverse weather and difficult terrain;
(c) the measures taken by Government to facilitate training of pilots, air traffic personnel and flight procedure specialists in advanced satellite-based navigation systems; and
(d) whether Government has a phased plan for satellite-guided aviation under the Regional Connectivity Scheme?

(a) whether Government has examined concerns relating to digitisation of land records and allegations of wrongful alterations affecting ownership rights of Scheduled Castes and Scheduled Tribes in certain parts of the country;
(b) the safeguards incorporated under the Digital India Land Records Modernization Programme (DILRM) to prevent unauthorised changes in land records;
(c) whether periodic social and technical audits of digital land records are being undertaken; and
(d) the measures taken to protect the land rights of vulnerable communities through transparent verification and grievance redressal mechanisms?

(a) whether Government has evaluated the preparedness of vehicles manufactured before mandatory E20-compatible standards for sustained use of E20 petrol;
(b) the directions issued to automobile manufacturers regarding durability assessment, replacement schedules and monitoring of rubber hoses, seals, gaskets and other fuel-system components exposed to higher ethanol blends;
(c) whether any long-term independent validation has been undertaken after commercial rollout to assess real-world vehicle performance; and
(d) the steps taken to promote affordable retrofitting, component upgrades and periodic public disclosure of technical performance assessment reports?

(a) whether Government has formulated a national programme to strengthen public libraries as centres for cultural engagement, film appreciation, literature and lifelong learning;
(b) the assistance extended to States for modernising libraries with facilities for screening educational and world cinema, digital archives and community learning activities;
(c) whether best practices adopted by successful public libraries are being documented for wider replication; and
(d) the initiatives taken to transform public libraries into vibrant knowledge and cultural resource centres across the country?

(a) whether Government has examined concerns arising from the implementation of TRAI's dedicated 140 and 1600 numbering series for commercial and service calls, particularly regarding consumer response and call completion rates;
(b) whether any review has been undertaken on the effectiveness of new numbering framework in reducing spam and fraudulent communications;
(c) the consultations held with telecom service providers, digital platforms and consumer organisations in this regard; and
(d) the measures proposed to balance consumer protection with uninterrupted delivery of legitimate commercial communications?

(a) whether Government has initiated a nationwide surveillance programme following the first reported detection of Parrot Bornavirus-4 (PaBV-4) in captive birds in the country;
(b) the biosecurity guidelines issued to zoological parks, aviaries, breeding centres and bird owners for preventing the spread of emerging avian viral diseases; 
(c) whether diagnostic facilities for early detection of such infections have been strengthened; and
(d) the measures taken to protect captive and endangered avian species through coordinated disease monitoring?

(a) whether Government has assessed the implications of nationwide E20 fuel availability for vehicles manufactured before E20 compatibility standards were introduced;
(b) the regulatory measures adopted to ensure that vehicle owners receive clear information regarding E20 compatibility, expected mileage, maintenance requirements and replacement of vulnerable fuel-system components;
(c) whether Government propose to issue uniform advisory guidelines requiring automobile manufacturers and dealers to prominently disclose E20 compatibility; and
(d) the measures proposed to strengthen consumer awareness, technical monitoring and periodic review during the transition to higher ethanol blending?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the potential for expanding solar-powered irrigation systems in Tamil Nadu to reduce dependence on conventional agricultural electricity connections and improve irrigation reliability;
(b) the details of financial assistance, subsidies and incentives extended by Government under various schemes for installation of standalone and grid-connected solar pumps in the State;
(c) the progress achieved in implementation of renewable energy-based irrigation solutions in Tamil Nadu; and
(d) the measures taken by Government to encourage farmers, cooperatives and farmer producer organisations to adopt solar-powered irrigation infrastructure?

(a) whether Government has taken cognisance of recent advances in genetic research highlighting variations in clinical manifestations of rare diseases arising from mutations in the same gene;
(b) the measures introduced for strengthening genetic diagnosis, genomic testing, early identification and personalised management of rare diseases through specialised healthcare institutions;
(c) the assistance provided for genomic research and rare disease diagnostics;
(d) the collaboration with medical research institutions and biotechnology organisations for advancing precision medicine; and
(e) the future plans for improving access to affordable diagnosis and treatment for patients with rare diseases?

(a) whether Government has assessed the impact of the decision to discontinue the proposed greenfield airport at Parandur on the long-term aviation capacity requirements of the Chennai metropolitan region;
(b) whether Government has identified or received proposals for an alternative site for Chennai's second airport;
(c) assistance proposed by Government for expediting statutory clearances, techno-economic studies and project approvals for the alternative location; and
(d) measures proposed to ensure that Chennai's future passenger and cargo growth is not constrained due to delays in developing additional airport infrastructure?

(a) whether Government is aware of studies indicating that continued dependence on Internal Combustion Engine (ICE) vehicles increases crude oil imports, foreign exchange outgo and energy insecurity in the country;
(b) if so, the details of Government’s assessment regarding the economic and energy implications of large-scale ICE vehicle usage;
(c) the details of incentives presently available for accelerating electric vehicle adoption;
(d) whether Government has evaluated the potential reduction in petroleum consumption through greater Electric Vehicle penetration; and
(e) the initiatives proposed to be taken by Government to promote cleaner and more energy-efficient mobility systems across the country?
GK

(a) the role envisaged by Government for agroforestry and tree-based farming systems in enhancing agricultural productivity, improving soil health, strengthening climate resilience and augmenting farmers' income across diverse agro-climatic regions of the country; 
(b) the schemes rolled out by Government for integrating trees within agricultural landscapes, including support for plantation activities, technical advisory services, quality planting material and capacity-building efforts for farmers; and 
(c) the initiatives proposed to be taken by Government to accelerate the adoption of agroforestry practices and mainstream them as an important pillar of climate-resilient agriculture in the country?

(a) whether Government has examined the recent international assessments indicating that a larger share of biodiversity finance is being channelled directly to indigenous peoples and local communities, recognising their significant contribution to conservation and sustainable management of ecosystems under the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework;
(b) the measures adopted by Government to ensure that biodiversity-related financial assistance reaches eligible forest-dwelling and tribal communities in a transparent, accountable and equitable manner;
(c) the institutional mechanism for community participation in deciding the utilisation of such funds; and
(d) the safeguards established to monitor outcomes and ensure effective conservation?
GK

(a) Government's assessment of the changing employment landscape resulting from the growing adoption of Artificial Intelligence (AI) across different sectors of the economy;
(b) the sectors identified for creating new employment opportunities through human-AI collaboration, technological innovation and productivity enhancement;
(c) the measures adopted for equipping workers with AI-related and digital skills;
(d) the collaboration with industry, educational institutions and skill development agencies for workforce preparedness; and
(e) the proposals under consideration for ensuring inclusive employment growth in the AI-driven economy?

(a) the importance attached to strengthening human-centric skills such as creativity, critical thinking, leadership, communication and teamwork in view of the growing adoption of Artificial Intelligence across industries;
(b) the programmes introduced for integrating behavioural, cognitive and interpersonal competencies with digital and Artificial Intelligence-related skills under national skill development initiatives;
(c) the support extended for preparing youth for AI-enabled workplaces;
(d) the collaboration with industry and academic institutions for redesigning skill development courses; and
(e) the future plans for developing a workforce equipped with both technological expertise and human capabilities?

(a) the vision of Government for transforming higher education to meet the learning and skill requirements of the Artificial Intelligence (AI) era;
(b) the reforms introduced for promoting research-oriented learning, project-based education, interdisciplinary studies and life long learning in higher educational institutions;
(c) the measures adopted for integrating Artificial Intelligence tools into teaching and learning while preserving critical thinking and academic integrity;
(d) the support extended for upgrading faculty capabilities in emerging technologies; and
(e) the action proposed for preparing students for rapidly evolving careers and future workplaces?

(a) whether Government has assessed the prevalence of infertility and reproductive health disorders among couples and introduced programmes for promoting awareness of the role of nutrition, stress management and early health screening for obesity, diabetes, thyroid disorder, etc., in preventing infertility;
(b) the policy framework evolved by Government to promote reproductive health awareness through timely fertility screening, preventive healthcare and lifestyle interventions through public health institutes;
(c) the collaboration established with State Governments for infertility awareness campaign and for expanding access to reproductive health counselling and early diagnosis; and
(d) the roadmap prepared to strengthen preventive reproductive healthcare services, particularly for young adults and newly married couples and in underserved areas?

(a) the details of Government's assessment regarding diversification of Liquefied Petroleum Gas (LPG) import sources through increased purchases from the United States to strengthen the country's energy security and reduce excessive dependence on any single region;
(b) the factors considered by Government while determining the future import mix between the Gulf region, the United States and other supplying countries;
(c) the likely impact on domestic LPG availability and price stability;
(d) the coordination with public sector oil marketing companies for procurement planning; and
(e) the expected benefits for long-term energy resilience and uninterrupted fuel supplies?

(a) whether Government has taken note of reports attributing recurring fires, building collapses, stampedes and other urban disasters to congestion, unsafe construction and weak enforcement of planning regulations;
(b) the findings of Government regarding deficiencies in urban planning and municipal governance;
(c) whether a nationwide review of compliance with the National Building Code and fire safety norms has been conducted;
(d) whether mandatory periodic safety audits of public buildings are under consideration; and
(e) the measures proposed to decongest cities, strengthen disaster preparedness and ensure accountability for preventable urban disasters?

(a) whether Government has formulated a strategy for addressing the challenge of stray dog populations and their implications for public safety, animal welfare and disease control across the country;
(b) if so, the mechanisms put in place by Government to support sterilization, anti-rabies vaccination and scientific management of stray dogs and if not, the reasons therefor;
(c) the extent of dog-bite cases, rabies-related concerns and public health risks associated with increasing stray dog populations across the country; and
(d) the initiatives proposed to be taken by Government to strengthen humane population management and improve public safety?

(a) whether Government has assessed the growing impact of recurring heatwaves on school-going children, particularly in view of rising temperatures and recent measures such as water reminder systems introduced in educational institutions;
(b) if so, the details of measures undertaken by Government in coordination with the Tamil Nadu State Government and other States to protect students through revised school timings, hydration protocols, cooling infrastructure and heat safety advisories; and
(c) the initiatives proposed to be taken by Government to develop long-term heat resilience measures for schools and educational institutions across the country?

(a) whether Government has explored the potential of Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) resources to support innovation, social enterprises and mission-driven organizations capable of delivering scalable social impact across the country;
(b) if so, the framework developed by Government to encourage deployment of CSR resources towards research, innovation, technology development and social entrepreneurship initiatives and if not, the reasons therefor; and
(c) the initiatives proposed to be taken by Government to strengthen innovation financing and support growth of high-impact non-profit enterprises in the country?

(a) the factors contributing to the recent decline in domestic fertilizer production in the country, particularly in the context of global supply disruptions, rising input costs and dependence on imported raw materials;
(b) the details of measures undertaken by Government for addressing production constraints, ensuring adequate availability of fertilizers and stabilising supply chains for the agricultural sector;
(c) the progress made in strengthening domestic fertilizer manufacturing, improving raw material security and supporting uninterrupted supply of fertilizers to farmers; and
(d) the initiatives proposed by Government for enhancing domestic production capacity, reducing import dependence and safeguarding agricultural productivity?

(a) whether Government is aware that despite rising solar output, coal remains the backbone of electricity generation during non-solar hours and increasing evening demand is placing additional pressure on thermal plants;
(b) if so, the coal stock availability at thermal plants during the current summer season;
(c) the thermal plants maintenance schedules deferred to meet rising summer demand;
(d) whether Government proposes thermal plants flexibility reforms, operational improvements, and technological upgrades to complement renewable energy expansion; and
(e) the initiatives proposed by Government to maintain uninterrupted thermal power generation during peak demand periods?

(a) Government's assessment of the increasing commercial adoption of drone technologies in security, infrastructure inspection, logistics, precision agriculture and service-based delivery models, supported by growing investor interest and regulatory support; 
(b) the policy interventions, certification reforms and facilitation measures undertaken by Government to improve market access, competitiveness and export potential of domestic drone enterprises; 
(c) the initiatives proposed by Government to strengthen training, testing and certification capacities for the drone sector; and 
(d) the measures proposed by Government to promote innovation, skilled employment generation and wider integration of drone solutions across the country?
